{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Third plan-review remediation: replaced the impossible deterministic-behavior proxy with the shipped live criterion-eval path ( via ). Planned a balanced four-case corpus that proves the transient private-probe exclusion, protects durable findings from over-suppression, and preserves b2 for untrusted-network transient services. Added an offline text/fixture-shape oracle, a direct negative oracle for T15 references, and updated file impact. The P7 wording remains descriptive rather than an operation; P6 was addressed by atomizing every eval outcome into its own AC."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786552008328471001,"uuid":"6736f19e-9adf-4d6a-80cf-080e32222ce3"}